Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Compile the pool allocator against one freestanding shim
Upstream: APR 1.7.4
Upstream-Archive: https://archive.apache.org/dist/apr/apr-1.7.4.tar.gz
Upstream-SHA256: a4137dd82a185076fa50ba54232d920a17c6469c30b0876569e1c2a05ff311d9
Build-Variants: native port, Capstone domain
Depends-On: none
Apply-From: upstream source root, with patch --batch --forward --fuzz=0 -p1

apr_pools.c and the two headers carrying its types include fourteen APR
headers, two of them generated by configure -- a host build this port does not
have and does not want. Replace every one with adapted/apr_shim.h, which
declares what the allocator asks for and nothing else, and sets the two flags
that decide how much of it survives (APR_HAS_THREADS, APR_ALLOCATOR_USES_MMAP)
to zero, as the census does. The allocator itself is untouched: this patch
removes twenty-one include lines and adds three.

This is the census seam, recorded as a patch so the prepared source is
reproducible from the archive and the patch alone, rather than from a script.

